   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Children and teenagers, building resilience and promoting their rights in districts of northern Lima</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This new project aims to build on past work by aiming to strengthen the opportunities for children and teenager participation at community and district levels, as active citizens, and in community and government initiatives to reduce risks and violence against children and teenagers. The project will focus on the next phase of developing meaningful participation for young people, which will be achieved through two new elements: supporting children and adolescents to develop personal life plans - which has the dual objective of enabling young people to tackle risks and enable conditions for personal, family and social wellbeing - and to exercise their active citizenship and to strengthen community action and local governance systems led with as well as for children and adolescents.
The project will focus primarily on four rights: education, protection, participation, and a healthy environment.</narrative>
  </description>
